# Animate Dead: "When this Aura leaves the battlefield, that creature's controller sacrifices it." Bot1 kills its own
# Ornithopter with Cut Down and brings it back with Animate Dead on turn 1 (a 0/2 that is a -1/2 under the Aura); on turn 2
# Bot2 Disenchants the Aura. The Aura leaving is what sacrifices the Ornithopter, so it goes to its owner's graveyard
# (CR 701.21a, 603.6c). The Ornithopter stays on the battlefield until then - nothing else removes it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Ornithopter
Cut Down
Animate Dead
Swamp
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Disenchant
Plains x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cut Down.Cast(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Animate Dead.Cast(Bot1.Graveyard.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = -1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 2
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Disenchant.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Animate Dead)
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp; Mox Jet; Mox Pearl
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Animate Dead; Cut Down
Bot2.Graveyard = Disenchant
